WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
- [Kelly] Ya'll both
have such a great song.

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.273
You know each other?

00:00:02.273 --> 00:00:03.251
- [People] Yes we do.

00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:04.084
- I was like, if that's how

00:00:04.084 --> 00:00:05.933
you embrace a stranger, it's incredible.

00:00:05.933 --> 00:00:07.530
(audience laughing)

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.970
Well, how's your new year going?

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:09.990
- My new year's going...

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:10.823
I'm just...

00:00:10.823 --> 00:00:11.656
I'm on a Kelly Clarkson show, come on.

00:00:11.656 --> 00:00:12.489
(Kelly exclaiming in excitement)

00:00:12.489 --> 00:00:13.374
(audience cheering)

00:00:13.374 --> 00:00:14.357
It started very, very well.

00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:15.330
- It started off well, yeah.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.363
- Beautiful. No, it's an
amazing New Year for me.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.810
I feel like I'm living into the dreams

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.250
I had as a kid now.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.537
- Beautiful.
- [Ami] You know?

00:00:24.537 --> 00:00:26.700
And so, when that happens in your life,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.920
and now you're in a
realities, it's very strange.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.000
You're just trying to stay in the moment

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.980
as much as possible and take it in.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.390
- Take it in, yeah.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.550
So what do you think,
like, playing Dr. King,

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.739
like, what did that teach you?

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:38.835
Like, what did you learn from that?

00:00:38.835 --> 00:00:39.668
(indistinct)

00:00:39.668 --> 00:00:40.920
- As much as I'm having a great year now,

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.510
last year was crazy difficult.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.700
Had loads of losses, and family losses.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.860
And when I was actually...

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.420
When I was playing the character,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.947
one of my favorite
speeches by him was, like,

00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:52.650
"Any man I'd like to live a long life,

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.210
longevity has his place.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.200
But I'm not worried with that now,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.730
I'm trying to do god's will."

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.570
And that really shaped my life, actually.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.310
Kind of leaning into that,

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.110
you're not gonna always be in
control of things, you know?

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.498
Things change a lot.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.320
- Isn't it freeing, though,
when you let go of that?

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.190
When you try and...
- You let go of it,

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.023
and you just...

00:01:09.023 --> 00:01:10.740
You allow life and whatever you believe in

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.760
to guide you in a new way.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:12.760
So that was...

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.360
That's what I've kind of taken from

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.760
having the honor of playing
Dr. King, you know? It's...

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.680
- I know. Did you feel, like...?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.553
- Scared?
- [Kelly] (laughs) Yeah.

00:01:20.553 --> 00:01:22.140
- Yeah! Yeah!
- I was like...

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.107
If somebody was just like,

00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:24.060
"I want you to play..."

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.380
I would be like, "No!"

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.660
- Yeah, no, I'm a British
boy from North London.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.920
You know, you're like, "Oh, my goodness,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.537
they want me to play Dr. King?"

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.590
But, you know, I got
really blessed, lucky.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.920
George C. Wolfe saw
something in me, and...

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.270
- [Kelly] Very talented as well.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.629
Talent had to do with it.
- That's kind of you.

00:01:40.629 --> 00:01:42.300
It's very kind of you. And it was like...

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.830
You know, it was that opportunity

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.800
to step into what you've been trying

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.150
to cultivate your entire life.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.320
You're an actor, you know?

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.870
We work, and we're waiting for that moment

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.450
to really step into something powerful,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.580
and to play someone that is iconic,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.520
but find a grounded way of
kind of attaching to them.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.050
You found that with
Aretha, I'm sure, right?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:01.941
- Yeah, yeah, that was...

00:02:01.941 --> 00:02:04.794
So it was definitely that moment for me.

00:02:04.794 --> 00:02:07.140
- Well, we're celebrating
music as a movement,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.790
so music's...

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.947
But that's gotta be important
in your life, right?

00:02:09.947 --> 00:02:10.780
- [Ami] Oh, music. Everything.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.613
- You're too passionate!
You came out here,

00:02:11.613 --> 00:02:12.473
I was like, "He likes music."

00:02:12.473 --> 00:02:15.900
- As soon as they hit the
thing, I was like, "Oh, what?"

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.551
- So what do you like to listen to?

00:02:17.551 --> 00:02:20.310
- Oh, my taste is eclectic. From, like...

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.858
We can go, like, Fela Kuti...

00:02:21.858 --> 00:02:22.691
(Jennifer grunting in surprise)

00:02:22.691 --> 00:02:24.630
We can go, you know, GIXX. We can...

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.463
(Ami laughing)
- She made a sound.

00:02:25.463 --> 00:02:26.850
An actual, just guttural sound.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:30.240
- Marvin Gaye. Listen,
I did musicals as a kid.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.510
Like, I played Little Sammy
Davis Jr. in "The Jolson Story."

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.830
And Oliver. I'm actually...

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.149
My next film as a director
will be directing a musical.

00:02:38.149 --> 00:02:38.982
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh, that's awesome!

00:02:38.982 --> 00:02:39.815
(Ami tongue-clucking)

00:02:39.815 --> 00:02:40.648
- Okay. Alright. I see you.

00:02:40.648 --> 00:02:42.254
(people laughing)

00:02:42.254 --> 00:02:43.331
- [Kelly] Wait, that's incredible!

00:02:43.331 --> 00:02:44.396
- You know me!
- [Kelly] Is this...?

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:45.888
- Gotta put pressure on her now!

00:02:45.888 --> 00:02:48.435
(people exclaiming in excitement)

00:02:48.435 --> 00:02:49.814
- [Kelly] Wait, is this one
of the dreams you're saying

00:02:49.814 --> 00:02:51.165
you've had since you were a kid,

00:02:51.165 --> 00:02:51.998
that you're now getting to step into?

00:02:51.998 --> 00:02:54.060
- Yeah. I got an opportunity to direct

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.580
my first feature film
a year-and-a-half ago.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.410
And I'm getting another
opportunity to direct, like,

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.250
a much bigger feature film,
and it's set around music,

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.290
It's set around music, and...

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.000
Yeah, so, I'm excited.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.538
Like, and in it is kind of
"Portuguese Love" by Teena Marie.

00:03:10.538 --> 00:03:11.860
(Jennifer exclaiming in surprise)

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.660
(indistinct)

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.870
- [Kelly] She leaned! She did a...

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.620
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.125
- And I... Your voice would be perfect.

00:03:18.125 --> 00:03:20.759
(indistinct)

00:03:20.759 --> 00:03:22.540
(people applauding)

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.787
- I know. You're now offering this,

00:03:23.787 --> 00:03:26.100
and I wanna introduce her
singing at the Oscars.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:26.933
We're just putting

00:03:26.933 --> 00:03:27.766
in our things.
- It's just happening.

00:03:27.766 --> 00:03:28.599
Like, we'll make it happen.
- We're putting in.

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:29.432
our things, yes.

00:03:29.432 --> 00:03:30.600
- Wait, I heard that when you were a kid,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.980
you were around, like, 11

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.710
when you worked with Michael
Jackson? That's crazy!

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:38.340
- So it was 1996. Mel's 11 years old,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.660
and I'm there like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.640
Like here, like, "Oh, my
god, this is amazing."

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.757
And this guy comes up and goes,

00:03:42.757 --> 00:03:44.400
"Alright, Michael
Jackson's about to come in.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.040
Nobody talk to Michael.
Don't even look at Michael!

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.110
Don't even..." And I'm like, "Okay."

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.406
So all of a sudden, the doors open.

00:03:50.406 --> 00:03:51.240
(Ami mimicking door opening)

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.380
And this guy comes in...
- And you hear...

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.355
(Kelly mimicking Michael
Jackson's singing)

00:03:53.355 --> 00:03:54.188
And it's like...

00:03:54.188 --> 00:03:55.230
(people laughing)

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.790
- There's bodyguards all around him.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.458
He's in this white robe. He's
coming through like this.

00:03:58.458 --> 00:03:59.291
- Of course he's in a robe.

00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:00.519
And then, all of a sudden,
he jumps on the stage.

00:04:00.519 --> 00:04:01.620
(Ami mimicking shoes
clattering on the floor)

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:02.453
I'm like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:04:02.453 --> 00:04:04.177
And then, he leans down
to me, and he goes,

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.490
"Why is everybody so quiet?"

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:06.960
And he has a deep voice.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:07.793
- [Kelly] What?

00:04:07.793 --> 00:04:09.394
- Michael Jackson
actually had a deep voice.

00:04:09.394 --> 00:04:10.227
(Jennifer laughing)

00:04:10.227 --> 00:04:11.060
I was like...

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.660
And he goes, "Hi, my name is Michael",

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.347
I'm like, "Yeah, I know."

00:04:14.347 --> 00:04:15.180
- [Kelly] "I'm aware."

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:16.013
(people laughing)

00:04:16.013 --> 00:04:17.810
"Yeah, I'm aware. I can't look
at you, sir." You're like...

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:20.010
- So that was the Brit Awards 1996,

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.258
famously when Jarvis Cocker came on stage.

00:04:22.258 --> 00:04:23.977
- Oh, my gosh, you were there!

00:04:23.977 --> 00:04:24.810
- I was the little boy in the...

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:25.643
(indistinct)

00:04:25.643 --> 00:04:27.614
- [Kelly] Wait, what happened?
- That's so crazy! Of course!

00:04:27.614 --> 00:04:28.536
- [Ami] Yeah, it was me!

00:04:28.536 --> 00:04:29.578
- Wait, what happened?

00:04:29.578 --> 00:04:31.506
- Oh my, I did not know that!

00:04:31.506 --> 00:04:32.411
- Yes! I was there.

00:04:32.411 --> 00:04:33.357
I've been around for a while.
- I didn't see it!

00:04:33.357 --> 00:04:35.097
Someone tell me what happened?

00:04:35.097 --> 00:04:35.930
(audience laughing)

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.005
- You can watch it on YouTube, everyone.

00:04:37.005 --> 00:04:38.520
- Oh, my gosh.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.980
- I'm there. I'm a little
boy, I've got a turban on,

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.410
and I'm standing right
next to Michael Jackson.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.240
Jarvis Cocker jumps on stage.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.830
He's singing the "Earth Song."

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:47.670
And he shows his...

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:48.503
I don't know if we can say this.

00:04:48.503 --> 00:04:49.336
Bottom? Is that okay to say?

00:04:49.336 --> 00:04:50.169
- [Jennifer] Yep.

00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:51.414
- Shows his ass.
- Bottom.

00:04:51.414 --> 00:04:52.247
(people laughing)

00:04:52.247 --> 00:04:53.100
Shows his ass.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.190
And kind of mocking Michael Jackson.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:59.610
Then everybody jumps on stage,
and running around, and...

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.640
The bottles flew, and people
got hit in their face, and...

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.473
- It was wild.

00:05:03.473 --> 00:05:05.370
- It was crazy, and I was one of the kids

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.190
that didn't get hit, but I
cried like I did get hit,

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.719
'cause I thought, "I
could get a deal here."

00:05:09.719 --> 00:05:11.806
(people laughing)

00:05:11.806 --> 00:05:13.490
Like, "Something could
happen." I was like,

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:15.877
"Oh! I'm hurt too!"
- [Kelly] "Oh, my god!

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.207
I'm injured! Where's my money?"

00:05:18.207 --> 00:05:21.330
- And Michael Jackson ended
up taking all those kids

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.930
to a place called Brent Cross
Shopping Centre, for any...

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.449
- [Jennifer] Nice.
- You would know.

00:05:26.449 --> 00:05:28.032
And got everybody PlayStations.

00:05:28.032 --> 00:05:28.865
- What?

00:05:28.865 --> 00:05:29.698
- What?

00:05:29.698 --> 00:05:31.227
- I never got the
PlayStation, but you know...

00:05:31.227 --> 00:05:33.348
(people laughing)

00:05:33.348 --> 00:05:34.187
- Sorry!

00:05:34.187 --> 00:05:35.340
- [Ami] You know?

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.500
- Well, we need to do a short
commercial break, everybody.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.333
You can see "Rustin" on Netflix.

